      "saw35_s6_d": "Longitudinal shell seams",
      "saw35_faq_label": "FAQ",
      "saw35_faq_h2": "Submerged arc welding FAQ",
      "saw35_q1": "What is submerged arc welding?",
      "saw35_a1": "Submerged arc welding (SAW, ISO 4063-121) is an automated arc process in which the arc between a continuously fed wire and the workpiece burns beneath granular flux. The flux shields the arc and weld pool and gives high deposition and deep penetration.",
      "saw35_q2": "What does a 35 m SAW machine offer?",
      "saw35_a2": "Long parts can be welded in a single set-up. Speed and parameters stay constant along the seam, so quality is repeatable, stop-start points and their defect risk drop, and repositioning time is cut.",
      "saw35_q3": "Which parts suit submerged arc welding?",
      "saw35_a3": "Medium and heavy steel parts with long, straight seams that can be welded flat (PA) or as horizontal fillets (PB): booms, chassis members, welded I-girders, box columns, plate butt joints and tank shells. MAG is the better choice for very short seams and thin sheet.",
      "saw35_q4": "Do you offer subcontract SAW?",
      "saw35_a4": "Yes. We weld booms, chassis and long-seam parts for your products to your drawings. Parts can come in for welding only, or be quoted as complete fabrication including cutting, bending, welding and NDT.",
      "saw35_q5": "What do you need for a quote?",
      "saw35_a5": "A drawing (PDF/DXF/STEP), material grade and thickness, seam lengths, quantity and, if any, the quality class (EN 1090 EXC, EN ISO 5817) and NDT requirements.",
      "saw35_blog_label": "Technical guides",
      "saw35_cta_h2": "Let's review your long-seam parts together",
